0,Indigenous music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_music_of_Australia,"Indigenous music of Australia comprises the music of the Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples of Australia, intersecting with their cultural and ceremonial observances, through the millennia of their individual and collective histories to the present day. [1][2][3][4] The traditional forms include many aspects of performance and ...",Kimaragang,Austronesian
1,"Kimaragang - Wikipedia Bahasa Melayu, ensiklopedia bebas",https://ms.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimaragang,"Kimaragang ialah kelompok Dusunik atau orang asli yang mendiami sebahagian besar bukit dan lembah di Kota Marudu dan daerah Pitas [1]. Seluruh kawasan Tandek di Kota Marudu dihuni oleh etnik ini termasuk di Tingkalanon, Ulu Bangkoka, Samparita, Damai, Taritapan, Tondig, Togudon, Mosolog, Salimandut, Tinogu, dan Tanjung Batu.",Kimaragang,Austronesian
2,Traditional Music by Kimaragang from Kota Marudu - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bbue18t_bRI,"Beautiful melodies of traditional music by Kimaragang tribe from Kota Marudu, the northern part of Sabah, Malaysia. Bravo to the team from Persatuan Kimaragg...",Kimaragang,Austronesian
3,The Pinakang Dance of the Kimaragang People - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HsMDsqEP4bk,"The Pinakang dance is a traditional performance of the Kimaragang ethnic group, a sub-ethnic group of the Dusun who primarily reside in the Kota Marudu and Pitas districts of Sabah, Malaysia.",Kimaragang,Austronesian
4,Pinakang is the most representative traditional dance of the Kimaragang ...,https://www.facebook.com/VisitBorneo/videos/pinakang-is-the-most-representative-traditional-dance-of-the-kimaragang-people-w/866474913176886/,"Pinakang is the most representative traditional dance of the Kimaragang people, who reside in Kota Marudu, northern Sabah. Accompanied by the bright, crisp rhythm of the Kulintangan and the deep, resonant tones of the Gong, the dancers move slowly and gracefully. They sway and turn to the melodious rhythm like flora gently rustling in a breeze.",Kimaragang,Austronesian
5,Traditional Music by Kimaragang from Kota Marudu,https://www.facebook.com/VisitBorneo/videos/1726765587751447/,"Beautiful melodies of traditional music by Kimaragang tribe from Kota Marudu, the northern part of Sabah, Malaysia. Bravo to the team from Persatuan Kimaraggang Sabah (Kota Marudu). #sabah #malaysia...",Kimaragang,Austronesian
6,Kimaragang,https://www.kimaragang.net/en,"Welcome. This website is a repository for written and audio materials in the Kimaragang language. For those who do not know Kimaragang, we have translated as many materials as possible into Malay and English. How to Contribute Written Materials to This Site If you would like to contribute a folktale or other types of written materials to this site, we are happy to receive and post your ...",Kimaragang,Austronesian
7,Tarian Pinakang Etnik Kimaragang Di Sabah: Analisis Makna Dan Falsafah,https://erepo.usm.my/entities/publication/9bd456aa-53f1-41ab-8ea6-0a8d5e0a11de,"Tarian Pinakang merupakan salah satu daripada tarian tradisional etnik Kimaragang yang banyak dipersembahkan di kawasan Daerah Kota Marudu, dan beberapa kawasan di Daerah Pitas, Sabah. Kajian ini bertujuan bagi mengenal pasti dan memahami fungsi tarian ini, serta mendalami makna dan falsafah yang terkandung di dalam persembahan tarian Pinakang.",Kimaragang,Austronesian
8,Austronesian Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/austronesian-music,"Austronesian music is an umbrella term for the diverse musical traditions of Austronesian-speaking peoples, whose homelands stretch from Taiwan through Island Southeast Asia to Oceania and Madagascar.",Kimaragang,Austronesian
9,Ki Mara Gang | PDF,https://www.scribd.com/doc/155833460/Ki-Mara-Gang,"Ki Mara Gang Dokumen ini membincangkan tentang suku kaum Kimaragang di Sabah. Ia menyenaraikan beberapa tarian tradisional dan muzik yang terkenal di kalangan suku kaum ini seperti Tarian Pinakang, Mongigol, Memiluk serta alat muzik seperti tagung dan kulintangan.",Kimaragang,Austronesian
